/target

# `Cargo.lock` is deliberately *not* ignored.
#
# Cargo's rule is: ignore it for a library, commit it for a binary. This
# workspace ships binaries — `grasm`, and the runtime a `--native` build links
# against — so the lock file is what makes a build of tag `v1.0.0` today the
# same build in a year. Ignoring it meant CI resolved fresh versions on every
# run, which is the opposite of what a release tag promises.
.DS_Store
__pycache__/

# The security benchmark builds a throwaway Rust project to prove `std::fs` is
# ambient there. Its lock file is an artifact of running the gate, not source.
/benchmarks/security/rust/app/Cargo.lock
